# @zhoda/dsh-plugin conventions

- TypeScript strict mode, `pnpm`, React for UI panels.
- Thin shell only: the plugin calls zhoda-core (HTTP) or zhoda-mcp (SSE) and
  renders results. Zero deliberation logic in this package.
- Pin the dsh peer dependency; keep a compatibility matrix in the README.
  dsh is a developer preview — expect breaking changes.
- Feature flag `ZHODA_DSH_UI=off` must degrade the plugin to a pure
  tools provider if dsh UI slots change.
- The faction graph animates switches: a model moving factions is the
  signature visual — never render it as a static list.
- If the core is unreachable, show an honest "council offline" state with
  launch instructions (`uvx zhoda-mcp`), never a spinner forever.
